  "texts": {
    "preamble": "N.Kishore vs State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5086 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/accused seek to quash the proceedings against them in C.C.No.250 of 2018 in Crime No.35 of 2018 of Macherla Rural Police Station, Guntur District, which was registered against them for the offences under Sections 188, 273, 420, 120-B of IPC and Secs.58, 59 & 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 29.03.2018, the S.I of Police along with staff, on credible information rushed to the Gannavaram Cross road, Kambhampadu Village, seized banned tobacco products from the petitioners, later arrested them and registered a case in Crime No.35 of 2018 for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
